module haptotaxisDetection
module chemotaxisDetection
module competingGradientDetection

manifest PBS
manifest Fibronectin
manifest PluronicF127
manifest B4F_BiotinFluorescein
manifest StreptavidinCy3
manifest CCL21_24_98_bio
manifest CCL19
manifest FITCDextran_10kDa
manifest DendriticCells
manifest CellCultureMedium_R10

// ============================================================
// A Microfluidic Device for Measuring Cell Migration Towards
// Substrate-Bound and Soluble Chemokine Gradients.
// Schwarz, Bierbaum, Merrin, Frank, Hauschild, Bollenbach,
// Tay, Sixt, Mehling - Scientific Reports 6:36440 (2016).
// DOI: 10.1038/srep36440
//
// Protocol: Two-layer PDMS microfluidic device for simultaneous
// generation of (i) surface-immobilized haptotactic chemokine
// gradients (CCL21) via LAPAP photo-patterning and (ii) diffusion-
// based soluble chemotactic gradients (CCL19) via flow-switching
// source-sink strategy. Dendritic cells (DCs) derived from
// C57BL/6J mouse bone marrow are tracked at single-cell
// resolution in combined and competing chemokine gradient fields.
//
// Device geometry: 6 migration chambers per chip
//   l = 1100 um, w = 200 um, h_max = 28 um
//   9 reagent inlets, 1 cell loading inlet, 3 waste outlets
//   Independently controllable PDMS membrane valves on all ports
//   Support channels connect reagent inlets to migration chambers
//   Chambers coated with fibronectin (250 ug/mL) for beta2-
//   integrin-mediated DC adhesion and 2D migration.
//
// LAPAP (Laser-Assisted Protein Adsorption by Photobleaching):
//   UV laser (355 nm, pulsed, 20x objective, galvanometric mirrors)
//   photobleaches B4F (biotin-4-fluorescein) covalently deposited
//   on glass surface in arbitrary gradient patterns (~0.7 um
//   lateral resolution, ~100:1 dynamic range). Streptavidin-Cy3
//   bridges B4F to biotin-tagged CCL21 (CCL21 24-98 bio, truncated
//   to remove heparan-sulfate-binding C-terminus, avoiding
//   non-specific background).
//
// Soluble gradient generation: Flow-free diffusion via switching
//   source-sink channels at short ends of chamber. FITC-dextran
//   10 kDa used as proxy tracer (hydrodynamic radius 2.3 nm ~
//   CCL19 at 1.7+/-0.4 nm and CCL21 at 1.9+/-0.4 nm).
//   Peak CCL19 ~1.8 ug/mL at 2.5 h (Fig. 1d).
//
// NOTE ON BS ABSTRACTION:
//   LAPAP laser writing is abstracted as a `mix` of B4F coating
//   with PBS (wash step) to represent the photobleaching and
//   surface functionalization event. All channel flow and valve
//   actuation steps are abstracted via `mix` operations.
//   `heat` statements model temperature-controlled incubation
//   steps. Duration tokens: s and m only (BioScript constraint).
//   48 h = 2880 m; 10 min = 10m; 20 min = 20m; 30 min = 30m.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device prep, fibronectin coating,
//                              LAPAP patterning, CCL21 immobilization,
//                              DC loading, gradient generation
//   BB2  haptotaxisPass     -- haptotaxisSignal > 0: directed DC
//                              migration toward CCL21 gradient detected;
//                              dispose and proceed to chemotaxis branch
//   BB3  haptotaxisFail     -- haptotaxisSignal <= 0: no directed
//                              migration; drain
//   BB4  haptotaxisJoin     -- join: soluble CCL19 chemotaxis branch
//   BB5  chemotaxisPass     -- chemotaxisSignal > 0: directed DC
//                              migration toward CCL19 gradient detected;
//                              dispose and proceed to competing branch
//   BB6  chemotaxisFail     -- chemotaxisSignal <= 0: undirected; drain
//   BB7  chemotaxisJoin     -- join: competing gradient branch begins
//   BB8  competingPass      -- competingSignal > 0: differential
//                              directionality resolved; dispose all
//   BB9  competingFail      -- competingSignal <= 0: no resolution; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose QC signals, end
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Chip priming with PBS.
//   Flow lines pressurised at 0.2-0.4 bar. Entire chip filled
//   with PBS. Flow channels connected to reagent inlets.
//   Control channels actuated at 0.5 bar above baseline to
//   determine optimal closing pressure for each chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS1 = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPBS2 = dispense 1 units of PBS
chipPrime   = mix primingPBS1 with primingPBS2 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Fibronectin coating of migration chambers.
//   Human plasma fibronectin (c = 250 ug/mL, Millipore) loaded
//   into cell culture chambers via flow channels. Incubated for
//   1 h at room temperature. Fibronectin acts as beta2-integrin
//   ligand enabling DC adhesion and 2D migration on PDMS surface.
//   After 1 h, fibronectin in flow channels flushed with PBS.
//   Chambers then flushed with cell culture medium (R10) for 10 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectin      = dispense 1 units of Fibronectin
fibronectinCoat  = mix chipPrime with fibronectin for 60m

// Flush flow channels with PBS after coating.
pbsFlush1        = dispense 1 units of PBS
coatedChamber    = mix fibronectinCoat with pbsFlush1 for 1m

// Flush chambers with R10 medium for 10 min.
r10Medium1       = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
chamberReady     = mix coatedChamber with r10Medium1 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: LAPAP - B4F loading into migration chambers.
//   Chambers washed with PBS (10 s) to remove unbound fibronectin.
//   Biotin-4-fluorescein (B4F, 150 ug/mL, Sigma Aldrich) loaded
//   into assembled, closed channels via reagent inlets.
//   B4F coats the glass surface of the assembled chip
//   prior to UV laser patterning.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsWash1    = dispense 1 units of PBS
b4fSolution = dispense 1 units of B4F_BiotinFluorescein
b4fLoaded   = mix chamberReady with pbsWash1 for 10s
b4fCoated   = mix b4fLoaded with b4fSolution for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: LAPAP - UV laser gradient writing.
//   355 nm pulsed UV laser (Zeiss LD Plan Neo 20x/0.4 objective)
//   focused at glass-B4F interface. Galvanometric mirror pair
//   scans focus spot across chamber bottom. Pixel intensity image
//   specifies local light dose for gradient patterning.
//   Gradient written one spot at a time; spot spacing ~half focus
//   diameter for continuous pattern.
//   Lateral resolution: ~0.7 um. Dynamic range: ~100:1.
//   Laser pulse frequency: 1 kHz. Calibrated for off-center NA drop.
//   Pattern types: uniform patch (for haptokinesis control) or
//   linear gradient (for haptotaxis experiments).
//
//   NOTE: `mix` here abstracts the laser scanning event over the
//   B4F-coated chamber surface. No reagent mixing in DMF sense.
//   Unbound B4F washed out with PBS after laser writing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lapapPBS     = dispense 1 units of PBS
lapapPattern = mix b4fCoated with lapapPBS for 20m

// Wash unbound B4F from chambers after laser writing.
pbsWash2      = dispense 1 units of PBS
patternWashed = mix lapapPattern with pbsWash2 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Streptavidin-Cy3 (SA-Cy3) incubation.
//   SA-Cy3 (10 ug/mL in PBS with 3% BSA, Sigma Aldrich)
//   loaded into chambers and incubated for 20 min at RT.
//   Streptavidin binds to photobleached B4F anchors in the
//   laser-written pattern, serving as adapter for biotin-
//   coupled CCL21. SA-Cy3 fluorescence allows visualization
//   and quantification of the printed gradient pattern.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

saCy3Solution = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinCy3
saCy3Bound    = mix patternWashed with saCy3Solution for 20m

// Wash with PBS (10 s) to remove unbound SA-Cy3.
pbsWash3      = dispense 1 units of PBS
saCy3Washed   = mix saCy3Bound with pbsWash3 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: CCL21 24-98 bio immobilization.
//   Biotinylated truncated murine CCL21 (CCL21 24-98 bio;
//   custom synthesized by ALMAC, Craigavon, UK) at 250 ng/mL
//   in PBS loaded into chambers. Incubated 30 min at 37 C.
//   Biotin tag on CCL21 C-terminus binds streptavidin anchors
//   in the LAPAP-patterned gradient. Truncated version (aa 24-98)
//   used to prevent unspecific background via the basic C-terminal
//   extension of full-length CCL21 (aa 1-134).
//   Maximal surface density: 157 +/- 33 molecules/um2.
//   Supporting channels kept under constant PBS flow (0.2 bar)
//   during loading to prevent non-specific adsorption outside
//   cell culture chambers.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ccl21Solution   = dispense 1 units of CCL21_24_98_bio
ccl21Immobilized = mix saCy3Washed with ccl21Solution for 30m

// Wash chambers with PBS (10 s) to remove unbound CCL21.
pbsWash4         = dispense 1 units of PBS
ccl21Washed      = mix ccl21Immobilized with pbsWash4 for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: DC loading into migration chambers.
//   Bone marrow-derived DCs from C57BL/6J mice (C57BL6 strain),
//   harvested day 8-10 of GM-CSF culture and matured overnight
//   with LPS (200 ng/mL). DC suspension at 10 x 10^6 cells/mL
//   in R10 medium loaded via short-end ports of the migration
//   chambers. Loading via short ends produces a distribution
//   of cells along the chamber length.
//   Cells adhere loosely to fibronectin-coated PDMS surface
//   over ~30 min (Supplemental Movie S2). Round morphology
//   with constant protrusions under control conditions.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dcSuspension  = dispense 1 units of DendriticCells
r10Medium2    = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
dcLoaded      = mix ccl21Washed with dcSuspension for 1m
dcAdhered     = mix dcLoaded with r10Medium2 for 30m

// ============================================================
// HAPTOTAXIS ARM: DC migration on immobilized CCL21 gradient
// (without soluble gradient superimposition)
//
// STEP 8: CCL21 haptotaxis detection.
//   DCs imaged on Nikon Ti inverted microscope (10x/NA 0.3
//   and 20x/NA 0.5 Air Plan Fluor Ph1 objectives) with stage-top
//   incubator (37 C, 5% CO2, 90% humidity). EMCCD camera
//   (Hamamatsu C9100-02). Imaging area: 300 x 200 um
//   corresponding to CCL21 gradient pattern region.
//   Cell tracks analyzed with Fiji + Manual Tracking plugin
//   and Matlab 2013. Directionality = <cos(Theta)> where Theta
//   is angle between gradient direction and cell displacement.
//   Directionality bootstrapped 200x with original sample size.
//   Tracking interval: 3 min (cells move ~1 cell diameter).
//
//   Expected results (Fig. 3):
//   - No chemokine: undirected migration (rose plot isotropic)
//   - CCL21 patch (uniform): haptokinesis (increased speed,
//     no directed migration, rose plot isotropic)
//   - CCL21 gradient: haptotaxis (directed toward high [CCL21],
//     rose plot asymmetric toward gradient direction)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

haptotaxisSignal = detect haptotaxisDetection on dcAdhered for 100m

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Haptotaxis QC gate
// Pass (BB2): haptotaxisSignal > 0 -> directed DC migration
//             toward CCL21 gradient confirmed; dispose and
//             proceed to chemotaxis branch.
// Fail (BB3): haptotaxisSignal <= 0 -> no directional bias
//             (undirected or haptokinetic only); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (haptotaxisJoin).
// ============================================================

if (haptotaxisSignal > 0) {
    dispose dcAdhered
} else {
    drain dcAdhered
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: haptotaxisJoin
// Dispose haptotaxis QC signal. Control falls into soluble
// CCL19 chemotaxis branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose haptotaxisSignal

// ============================================================
// CHEMOTAXIS ARM: DC migration in soluble CCL19 gradient
// (no immobilized chemokine; diffusion-based gradient only)
//
// STEP 9: Fresh DC loading for chemotaxis experiment.
//   DCs loaded via short-end ports into fibronectin-coated
//   chambers (no CCL21 patterning). Cells distributed along
//   chamber length. 30 min adhesion recovery in R10 medium.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dcSuspension2  = dispense 1 units of DendriticCells
r10Medium3     = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
dcLoaded2      = mix r10Medium3 with dcSuspension2 for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: CCL19 soluble gradient generation.
//   Flow-free diffusion-based gradient generated by source-sink
//   flow-switching strategy (Frank & Tay, Lab Chip 13, 2013).
//   Source channel (one short end): sequentially refilled with
//   R10 + murine CCL19 (2.5 ug/mL; R&D Systems) + FITC-dextran
//   10 kDa (200 ug/mL, hydrodynamic radius 2.3 nm).
//   Sink channel (opposite short end): refilled with fresh R10.
//   Gradient builds by diffusion after flow stops; steepness,
//   mean concentration and duration independently controlled.
//   Peak CCL19 ~1.8 ug/mL after 2.5 h (Fig. 1d).
//   FITC-dextran traces gradient profile for quantification.
//   Control: R10 (no CCL19) from both ends (Fig. 4a).
//
//   Three CCL19 concentration regimes tested (Fig. 4b-d):
//   - CCL19_low:    0-1.2 ug/mL (chemokinetic, undirected)
//   - CCL19_medium: 0-1.3 ug/mL (directed chemotaxis)
//   - CCL19_high:   0-1.7 ug/mL (highly directional chemotaxis)
//
//   NOTE: Three replicate concentration regimes are encoded
//   sequentially. In practice these run in parallel in separate
//   migration chambers of the same chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ccl19Source     = dispense 1 units of CCL19
fitcDextran     = dispense 1 units of FITCDextran_10kDa
r10Sink         = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10

// Build CCL19/FITC-dextran source droplet for gradient.
ccl19FitcMix    = mix ccl19Source with fitcDextran for 5s

// Establish source-sink gradient across chamber.
gradientSetup   = mix dcLoaded2 with ccl19FitcMix for 5s
ccl19Gradient   = mix gradientSetup with r10Sink for 150m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: CCL19 chemotaxis detection.
//   DCs imaged as in STEP 8. Gradient direction and shape
//   indicated by FITC-dextran fluorescence. Cells tracked
//   from t=0 (gradient initiation) for up to 150 min.
//   Directionality plotted as function of chamber position
//   (= local CCL19 concentration; Fig. 4e):
//   - Low CCL19 (0-1.2 ug/mL): chemokinesis (faster, undirected)
//   - Medium CCL19 (0-1.3 ug/mL): significantly increased
//     directionality toward high [CCL19]
//   - High CCL19 (0-1.7 ug/mL): further augmented directionality
//   CCL19-concentration in gradients up to ~190 nM, covering
//   Kd of CCR7/CCL19 (10-100 nM) and sufficient for G-protein
//   loading and downstream signalling assays.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

chemotaxisSignal = detect chemotaxisDetection on ccl19Gradient for 150m

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Chemotaxis QC gate
// Pass (BB5): chemotaxisSignal > 0 -> directed DC migration
//             toward CCL19 gradient confirmed; dispose and
//             proceed to competing gradient branch.
// Fail (BB6): chemotaxisSignal <= 0 -> undirected or
//             chemokinetic only (CCL19 too low); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (chemotaxisJoin).
// ============================================================

if (chemotaxisSignal > 0) {
    dispose ccl19Gradient
} else {
    drain ccl19Gradient
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: chemotaxisJoin
// Dispose chemotaxis QC signal. Control falls into competing
// chemotactic + haptotactic gradient branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose chemotaxisSignal

// ============================================================
// COMPETING GRADIENTS ARM: DC migration in simultaneous
// opposing CCL19 (soluble, chemotactic) and CCL21
// (immobilized, haptotactic) gradients.
//
// STEP 12: Chip preparation with CCL21 gradient + DC loading.
//   CCL21-gradient printed in lower and middle area of migration
//   chamber via LAPAP (STEPS 3-6 protocol; maximal concentration
//   ~160 molecules/um2 = 0.24 ug/mL equivalent unit volume).
//   DCs loaded and positioned to include the two CCL21-gradient
//   regions. 30 min cell recovery post-loading.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Prepare new LAPAP-patterned CCL21 gradient (abbreviated;
// full patterning protocol as in STEPS 3-6 above).
pbsCompeting   = dispense 1 units of PBS
b4fCompeting   = dispense 1 units of B4F_BiotinFluorescein
saCy3Competing = dispense 1 units of StreptavidinCy3
ccl21Competing = dispense 1 units of CCL21_24_98_bio

b4fLoad2       = mix pbsCompeting with b4fCompeting for 1m
lapapWrite2    = mix b4fLoad2 with pbsCompeting for 20m
saCoat2        = mix lapapWrite2 with saCy3Competing for 20m
ccl21Coat2     = mix saCoat2 with ccl21Competing for 30m

// Load DCs into CCL21-patterned chamber.
dcSuspension3  = dispense 1 units of DendriticCells
r10Medium4     = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10
dcOnCCL21      = mix ccl21Coat2 with dcSuspension3 for 1m
dcRecovered    = mix dcOnCCL21 with r10Medium4 for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Opposing CCL19 soluble gradient superimposition.
//   After 30 min DC recovery on CCL21 gradient, diffusion-based
//   CCL19 gradient generated from the opposing direction to
//   the CCL21 gradient (Supplemental Figure S5).
//   Source: CCL19 + FITC-dextran at one short end (high [CCL19]).
//   Sink: R10 medium at opposite short end.
//
//   Two experimental conditions run in parallel on same chip
//   (one of each CCL21-gradient regions receives different
//   CCL19 concentration; Fig. 5):
//
//   Condition A - CCL19_low/CCL21 (Fig. 5a):
//     CCL19 source: 0-1 ug/mL opposing CCL21 gradient.
//     Expected: DC migration toward haptotactic CCL21 gradient
//     (CCL21 signal dominant at low soluble CCL19).
//
//   Condition B - CCL19_medium/CCL21 (Fig. 5b):
//     CCL19 source: 0-1.2 ug/mL opposing CCL21 gradient.
//     Expected: DC migration overrides toward chemotactic CCL19
//     (CCL19 signal dominant at medium concentration, overriding
//     haptotactic CCL21 directionality).
//
//   NOTE: Both conditions encoded sequentially below for CFG
//   clarity. Directionality measured as <cos(Theta)> vs.
//   position in channel and time (Fig. 5c).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Condition A: low CCL19 opposing CCL21 gradient.
ccl19LowSource    = dispense 1 units of CCL19
fitcDextran2      = dispense 1 units of FITCDextran_10kDa
r10SinkA          = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10

ccl19LowFitc      = mix ccl19LowSource with fitcDextran2 for 5s
conditionA        = mix dcRecovered with ccl19LowFitc for 5s
conditionAGrad    = mix conditionA with r10SinkA for 100m

// Condition B: medium CCL19 opposing CCL21 gradient.
ccl19MedSource    = dispense 1 units of CCL19
fitcDextran3      = dispense 1 units of FITCDextran_10kDa
r10SinkB          = dispense 1 units of CellCultureMedium_R10

ccl19MedFitc      = mix ccl19MedSource with fitcDextran3 for 5s
conditionB        = mix dcRecovered with ccl19MedFitc for 5s
conditionBGrad    = mix conditionB with r10SinkB for 100m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: Competing gradient detection and directionality
//   analysis.
//   DCs imaged as in STEP 8. Both SA-Cy3 (CCL21 gradient,
//   red) and FITC-dextran (CCL19 gradient, green) fluorescence
//   channels imaged simultaneously to confirm gradient
//   orientation and overlap.
//   Cell tracks analyzed for directionality over three time
//   windows (0-33, 33-66, 66-100 min) during CCL19 gradient
//   build-up phase (Fig. 5c).
//
//   Expected outcomes (Fig. 5):
//   - CCL19_low/CCL21: directionality toward CCL21 (haptotaxis
//     dominant at all time points; Fig. 5a, 5c right panel)
//   - CCL19_medium/CCL21: directionality switches toward CCL19
//     after gradient build-up (chemotaxis dominant; Fig. 5b,
//     5c left panel)
//   Interpretation: soluble CCL19 can override immobilized
//   CCL21 signal above a threshold concentration (~1 ug/mL).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

competingSignal = detect competingGradientDetection on conditionAGrad for 100m

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Competing gradient QC gate
// Pass (BB8): competingSignal > 0 -> differential directionality
//             between low and medium CCL19 conditions resolved;
//             dispose all droplets (experiment complete).
// Fail (BB9): competingSignal <= 0 -> no differential resolution
//             between conditions; drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (competingSignal > 0) {
    dispose conditionAGrad
    dispose conditionBGrad
} else {
    drain conditionAGrad
    drain conditionBGrad
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose competing gradient QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose competingSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
